  "body": {
    "id": "thm:network-schedule-reduction-answer",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every row-stochastic, outcome-free kernel \\(K\\) satisfying \\(d_K(A)\\geq\\pi(A)\\) for every nonempty \\(A\\subseteq\\Omega\\), the weak-order schedule handle has an exact finite-cell formulation.  It computes \\(p^{\\mathrm{wc}}_{r,c}(X)\\) and an optimizing compatible schedule, when one exists, by at most \\(2^N3^{m\\binom N2}\\) slack-certified linear feasibility problems.  For rational or real-algebraic inputs this computation terminates exactly; arbitrary real inputs admit only the corresponding ideal exact-real formulation.  The formulation solves the three-assignment shared-coordinate pattern and its nested inversion satisfies\n\\[\n \\ell_k(e;\\alpha)=b_k(X;\\alpha),\n \\qquad\n \\Pr_{X\\sim\\pi}\\!\\left\\{\\tau_{(k)}(e)\\geq\\ell_k(e;\\alpha)\n \\text{ for every }k=1,\\ldots,N\\right\\}\\geq1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nThe no-interference order-statistic interpretation and finite-sample validity of the two partition comparators are retained.  Exact recovery of the Caughey adjusted-outcome statistic and of the Su--Li multiple-choice-knapsack routine is false for the frozen assignment-specific score, as witnessed by the two-unit \\(1\\)-versus-\\(1/2\\) example.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "m",
      "N",
      "\\Omega",
      "\\pi",
      "X",
      "K",
      "d_K",
      "A",
      "p^{\\mathrm{wc}}_{r,c}",
      "r",
      "c",
      "\\ell_k(e;\\alpha)",
      "b_k",
      "e",
      "\\alpha",
      "\\tau_{(k)}(e)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:exact-network-schedule-reduction",
      "prop:no-interference-reduction"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "The exact finite-cell formulation, its bound of \\(2^N3^{m\\binom N2}\\) labels, attainment and infeasibility alternatives, exact-input qualifications, solution of the shared-coordinate pattern, projection identity, and simultaneous coverage are precisely the conclusions proved in \\(\\texttt{thm:exact-network-schedule-reduction}\\).  The final clauses of that theorem, proved through \\(\\texttt{prop:no-interference-reduction}\\), establish the no-interference order-statistic equivalence and partition-kernel validity and exhibit the stated \\(1\\)-versus-\\(1/2\\) counterexample.  Hence the open-ended question has the asserted positive answer for exact network schedule reduction and simultaneous inversion, and the asserted negative answer for exact recovery of the two comparator algorithms.",
